meta {
  name: PATCH Center Service Assignment V2
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{baseURL}}/centers/{{center_id}}/v2/services/{{service_id}}/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-Center-ID: {{center_id}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "duration": 30,
    "buffer_before": 5,
    "buffer_after": 10,
    "modality": "in_person",
    "required_room_type_ids": ["{{room_type_id}}"],
    "required_role_ids": []
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 30000
}

docs {
  Update per-center assignment config. modality: in_person | virtual | both.
  
  Body MUST be a JSON object { ... }. Pasting a bare UUID as the body → 400.
  
  All resource fields optional (omit = leave unchanged):
  - required_room_type_ids — UUID[] | null | [] (null/[] clears). OR eligibility for preferred room.
  - required_role_ids — UUID[] | null | [] (null/[] clears). Response always includes required_role_ids ([] when none) + nested required_roles.
  
  Response also includes required_room_types[] nested.
  
  Example with resources:
  {
    "duration": 30,
    "required_room_type_ids": ["01a03557-a6fd-74ea-a74a-e7db599aefa1"],
    "required_role_ids": []
  }
  
  Type UUIDs from GET room-types (not rooms). No equipment type on assignment.
  required_room_type_ids, required_role_ids must be active; inactive → 400.
  Set env service_id / room_type_id first. Omit or [] required_room_type_ids to clear.
}
